00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:33.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:33.267 --> 00:02:35.367
-I was going to say sexty,

00:02:35.367 --> 00:02:37.834
but I'll probably say a lot of
things like that.

00:02:37.834 --> 00:02:41.734
I've never been -- As you know,
I was born at 50, and I am

00:02:41.734 --> 00:02:45.334
a matron, and I did all the
old-lady parts in theater.

00:02:45.334 --> 00:02:46.868
And I just was always
the old lady.

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:49.434
So I always used to lecture
anyone that was going like,

00:02:49.434 --> 00:02:50.667
"Oh, my God, I'm going to
be 40,"

00:02:50.667 --> 00:02:52.834
and I'd be like,
"Numbers mean nothing."

00:02:52.834 --> 00:02:56.601
And now I'm completely losing my
mind about 60 because it just

00:02:56.601 --> 00:02:58.934
feels -- it does feel like
you're on the other end,

00:02:58.934 --> 00:03:01.734
kind of fading in the boat,
going...

00:03:01.734 --> 00:03:03.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.467 --> 00:03:05.100
"You guys have a wonderful
life."

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:07.334
-But you have a really nice
life.

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:09.300
-But I have such an incredible
life now.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:13.367
I moved from L.A. to the woods
of upstate New York,

00:03:13.367 --> 00:03:17.868
a little bit upstate, and we
live among all these crazy

00:03:17.868 --> 00:03:23.334
